# Ford Zephyr Mk IV four-door saloon, 1966-1972.
#
# The final Zephyr: the long flat bonnet, the squared wings and the wider
# track on the 2.921 m wheelbase. The pack photographs a Zephyr 4 (single
# headlamps, plain panel with FORD letters); the Zephyr 6 has a dummy grille
# panel and a Zephyr 6 badge.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Zephyr
#
# Dimensions 4.699 x 1.810 x 1.486 m, wheelbase 2.921 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation of a Zephyr 3008E;
# the front and rear three-quarters show the single lamps and the boot.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no 1966-72 chart was found. Blue, white, green and grey
# are plain names, not claimed as factory names. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12,
# total 60, provisional.
#
# Speed 155 km/h. Comfort 65/428, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 65. Classes 1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 1966 intro, retires staggered 1988-1991.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-zephyr-mk4.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-zephyr-mk4.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-zephyr-mk4/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the centre-panel recess, front corners and bumper wrap
# are simplified. At 128 px the long flat bonnet, single lamps and squared wings
# read as a Zephyr Mk IV.


obj=citycar
name=FordZephyrMk4(Blue)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=18
intro_year=1966
intro_month=4
retire_year=1991
retire_month=6
speed=155
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=65
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=428

